The 1931–32 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 44th season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish First Division]]<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1930/celtic1932.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1931-32|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> and the [[Scottish Cup]].

Celtic hoped to mount a challenge for the league title as they had ended last season only two points behind five-in-a-row winners [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]]. However, they ended up third, 18 points off champions [[Motherwell F.C.|Motherwell]], who had unsuccessfully challenged Celtic for the Scottish Cup in [[1931 Scottish Cup Final|the previous year's final]]. This was Motherwell's only league title as of 2025, and the first time someone other than the [[Old Firm]] won the league since 1904.

Celtic entered the Scottish Cup as title holders, but couldn't repeat the previous year's success as they lost to Motherwell 2-0 away in the third round.

